# COURSE_ID reference materials

> A textbook or a reference is registered once it has really been obtained; until then the table stays
> empty and no placeholder filename is written.
> A course with no primary textbook (goal / project / praxis driven) writes "no primary textbook" under
> "Primary textbook" and states where its evidence comes from.

## Primary textbook

| File | Material | Purpose |
|---|---|---|

Registration format:

```markdown
| `primary/Title_Edition_vol1.pdf` | Title, Nth edition, volume 1 (original PDF, size) | the book in use, advanced page by page each session |
| `primary/Title_Edition_vol1_text.pdf` | the OCR text layer of the same book (size) | source text is extracted through the preparation Snapshot + source_assets |
```

> **How the OCR text layer is used**: `_text.pdf` is the OCR result of the original PDF, keeping the text
> searchable and copyable.
> While teaching, the agent extracts the current page's text from `_text.pdf` into source_assets; it never
> transcribes by hand from the scanned original.

