## Usage rules

- **Primary textbook first**: each session extracts the current page's text from `_text.pdf`, delivers it
  through the preparation Snapshot + source_assets, and the agent teaches from the source text.
- A proof is governed by the textbook's own text; a reference book only supplies intuition.
- An exercise answer is for reference only and is never copied straight out — the student must think for
  the agreed time first.
- A reference of a different edition must note that its chapter numbering may not correspond.

## Adding external learning material

- Course-specific online material is registered in this README and never duplicated into the shared index.
- Cross-course material is classified per `main/50_playbook/book_management.md`, and only its resource ID
  and purpose from `main/40_course/_shared/external_resources.md` are referenced here.
- A temporary classroom page is managed through the preparation Snapshot; a file that genuinely needs
  offline sharing goes in `_shared/library/[resource-ID]/`.
